  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "📦 VDocs – Release Notes – HTML Shape Rendering Enhancements\n🚀 Version: 2026.6.1\n\n✨ Major Improvements to Shape-to-HTML Conversion\n\nThis release significantly enhances the HTML export engine with comprehensive support for rendering document shapes as native SVG elements.\n\n🎨 Expanded Shape Support\n - Added support for 250+ shape types during HTML export\n - Accurate rendering of:\n  - Basic shapes (rectangles, ellipses, triangles, diamonds)\n  - Arrows and connectors\n  - Stars and geometric shapes\n  - Flowchart symbols\n  - Brackets and callouts\n  - Action buttons and diagram elements\n  - And many more Word drawing shapes\n  \n🖌 Rich Visual Styling\nImproved preservation of shape appearance when exporting to HTML:\n - Solid fill colors\n - Linear gradient fills\n - Pattern and shading support\n - Outline colors and styles\n - Stroke dash patterns\n - Line caps and line joins\n - Rotation and positioning\n - Shape dimensions and scaling\n - Layer ordering (z-index)\n \n 📐 Enhanced SVG Generation\n - Shapes are now rendered as standards-compliant SVG elements\n - Custom path definitions are preserved when available\n - Intelligent path generation for built-in shape types\n - Improved rendering fidelity between Word documents and exported HTML\n \n🔄 Improved Layout Preservation\nShape transformation properties are now more accurately translated to HTML and SVG, including:\n - Positioning\n - Rotation\n - Scaling\n - Margins\n - Size and dimensions\n🛡 Reliability Improvements\n - Graceful fallback rendering for unsupported or custom shapes\n - Improved compatibility across modern web browsers\n - Reduced risk of rendering failures during HTML export\n \n📈 Result\nHTML exports now provide significantly higher visual fidelity for documents containing shapes, diagrams, callouts, flowcharts, and graphical elements, making exported documents closely match their original Word document appearance.\n\n🔧 Compatibility\n - No breaking API changes\n - Existing HTML export workflows remain fully compatible\n - Recommended update for users exporting documents containing shapes or diagrams",
  "requireLicenseAcceptance": true,
